 "context": "<div data-type=\"note\" data-has-label=\"true\" id=\"fs-id1166165469172\" class=\"interactive\" data-label=\"\">\n<h3 class=\"os-title\" data-type=\"title\"><span class=\"os-title-label\">PhET Explorations</span></h3>\n<div class=\"os-note-body\">\n<h4 data-type=\"title\" id=\"9\" class=\"os-subtitle\"><span class=\"os-subtitle-label\">PhET Explorations: Circuit Construction Kit (DC only)</span></h4>\n<p id=\"eip-829\" class=\" \">An electronics kit in your computer! Build circuits with resistors, light bulbs, batteries, and switches. Take measurements with the realistic ammeter and voltmeter. View the circuit as a schematic diagram, or switch to a life-like view.</p>\n<div class=\"os-figure\">\n<figure id=\"fs-id1166165257625\"><div data-type=\"media\" id=\"eip-idm415114672\" data-alt=\"This simulation is electronics kit in your computer.\">\n<div data-type=\"alternatives\" class=\"os-has-iframe os-has-link\">\n<a class=\"os-is-link\" target=\"_window\" href=\"https://openstax.org/l/21cirphysbascur\">Click to view content</a><iframe width=\"660\" height=\"371.4\" src=\"https://openstax.org/l/21cirphysbascur\" class=\"os-is-iframe\"><!-- no-selfclose --></iframe>\n</div>\n</div>\n</figure><div class=\"os-caption-container\">\n<span class=\"os-title-label\">Figure </span><span class=\"os-number\">21.42</span><span class=\"os-divider\"> </span>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>",
 "stimulus_html": "",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 239376,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "PhET Explorations: Circuit Construction Kit (DC only).\n\nAn electronics kit in your computer! Build circuits with resistors, light bulbs, batteries, and switches. Take measurements with the realistic ammeter and voltmeter. View the circuit as a schematic diagram, or switch to a life-like view.\n\n<iframe src=\"https://openstax.org/l/21cirphysbascu\"></iframe>",
   "stem_html": "When the circuit has reached the steady state, how does the voltage across the capacitor compare to the voltage of the battery? What is the voltage across the resistor?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 747076,
     "content_html": "The voltage across the capacitor is greater than the voltage of the battery. In the steady state, no current flows through this circuit, so the voltage across the resistor is zero."
    },
    {
     "id": 747075,
     "content_html": "The voltage across the capacitor is smaller than the voltage of the battery. In the steady state, finite current flows through this circuit, so the voltage across the resistor is finite."
    },
    {
     "id": 747077,
     "content_html": "The voltage across the capacitor is the same as the voltage of the battery. In the steady state, no current flows through this circuit, so the voltage across the resistor is zero."
    },
    {
     "id": 747074,
     "content_html": "The voltage across the capacitor is the same as the voltage of the battery. In the steady state, finite current flows through this circuit, so the voltage across the resistor is finite."
    }
   ],
